{%- set first = variants.0 -%}
# {{ theme.name }} tmux Theme

tmux themes for {{ theme.name }}. {{ theme.description }}

## Installation

### Plugin entry (recommended)

Set the variant and run the plugin entry from your `.tmux.conf`:

```tmux
set -g @{{ theme.id }}_variant '{{ first.variant.id }}'{% if variants | length > 1 %}  #{% for v in variants | slice(start=1) %} or '{{ v.variant.id }}'{% endfor %}{% endif %}
run-shell /path/to/{{ theme.id }}.tmux
```

### Manual

Source a variant's theme file in your `.tmux.conf` instead; the options below then do not apply:

```tmux
source-file /path/to/{{ theme.id }}-{{ first.variant.id }}.conf
```

## Variants

{% for v in variants -%}
- **{{ theme.id }}-{{ v.variant.id }}** - {{ v.variant.description }}
{% endfor %}
## Features

### Prefix Indicator

The status bar icon changes when you press the prefix key:

- 󰛩 - Normal mode (outline)
- 󰛨 - Prefix mode (filled)

## Options

| Option | Default | Description |
|--------|---------|-------------|
| `@{{ theme.id }}_variant` | `{{ first.variant.id }}` | Theme variant (`{{ first.variant.id }}`{% for v in variants | slice(start=1) %} or `{{ v.variant.id }}`{% endfor %}) |
| `@{{ theme.id }}_icon_normal` | `󰛩` | Icon shown in normal mode |
| `@{{ theme.id }}_icon_prefix` | `󰛨` | Icon shown when prefix is pressed |

### Example: Custom Icons

```tmux
set -g @{{ theme.id }}_icon_normal ''
set -g @{{ theme.id }}_icon_prefix ''
```
